<title>INDIA: India HDFC Bank cuts prime rate to 16 pct.</title>
<headline>India HDFC Bank cuts prime rate to 16 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>HDFC Bank said on Tuesday it will cut its prime lending rate to 16.0 percent per annum from 17.0 percent from May 1.</p>
<p>The revised rate is exclusive of interest tax, a bank official told Reuters.</p>
<p>The rate cut follows measures announced by the Reserve Bank of India to reduce deposit rates in its monetary policy for first half 1997/98 (April-March) released on April 15.</p>
<p>The official said the bank's deposit rates effective April 29 are as follows:</p>
<p>Maturity			   Interest (percent per annum)</p>
<p>----------------- ---------------------------- </p>
<p>30-45 days			     8.0</p>
<p>46-90 days			     8.5</p>
<p>91 days up to one year	     9.0</p>
<p>Over one year up to 18 months   11.5</p>
<p>Over 18 months up to five years 12.0</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
